---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate, getPosts } from '../lib/posts';

const latest = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 3);
---

<Base
  title="Yahia Ali Abusaif — Software Engineer"
  description="Senior software engineer. .NET and AWS backends, from 0-to-1 multi-tenant SaaS to systems already running at scale."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <img src="/profile.png" alt="Portrait of Yahia Ali Abusaif" width="96" height="96" />
    <div>
      <h1>Yahia Ali Abusaif</h1>
      <p class="role">Senior Software Engineer</p>
      <p class="lede">
        Senior software engineer with 5 years building .NET and AWS backends, from 0-to-1
        multi-tenant SaaS to systems already running at scale. At Microsoft, owned a
        cross-team workstream on a 500k+ domain pipeline: 90% less unnecessary data I/O,
        P0/P1 from 3-5 days to under 6 hours, and 600% editorial throughput. At Sahl,
        end-to-end owner of the B2C mobile and backend path through 40x transaction
        growth (2.5k to 100k/day). Now at Qualiphi, technical lead across two pods
        (greenfield SaaS and legacy), with a Design-First practice of ADRs and design
        docs. Known for workstream ownership, mentoring, and making the design explicit
        before the code.
      </p>
      <p class="meta-links">
        <span>New Cairo, Egypt · open to relocation</span>
        <a href="mailto:yahiaali2014.ya@gmail.com">yahiaali2014.ya@gmail.com</a>
        <a href="tel:+201030344226">+20 10 30344226</a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/yahiaabusaif" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/YahiaAbusaif" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://heylink.me/yahiaali2014.ya/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Heylink</a>
        <a href="/blog/">Writing</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="writing-heading">Latest writing</h2>
      <a href="/blog/">All writing</a>
    </div>
    <ol class="post-list">
      {
        latest.map((post) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>{post.data.title}</a>
            <time datetime={post.data.date.toISOString()}>{formatDate(post.data.date)}</time>
            {post.data.description && <p class="excerpt">{post.data.description}</p>}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
    <h2 id="skills-heading">Technical profile</h2>
    <ul class="skill-list">
      <li><strong>Languages & frameworks:</strong> C# (.NET Core), Dart (Flutter), Python (Django), React, SQL</li>
      <li><strong>Cloud & infrastructure:</strong> AWS (CDK, SQS, EventBridge, Lambda), Azure, Docker, CI/CD</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data & AI engineering:</strong> PostgreSQL, MS SQL, Entity Framework (EF), DynamoDB, Cosmos DB,
        Redis, Azure Data Factory, ETL pipelines, LLM integration
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Systems architecture:</strong> Domain-Driven Design, event-driven, multi-tenant SaaS,
        system migration, idempotency patterns
      </li>
      <li><strong>Observability & security:</strong> Grafana, New Relic, design docs, ADRs, RFCs</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-heading">Professional experience</h2>

    <article class="job">
      <h3>Senior Software Engineer — Qualiphi (Cairo, Egypt)</h3>
      <p class="when">Nov 2025 – Present</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Greenfield technical leadership:</strong> Acted as primary technical lead for a
          complete 0-to-1 platform expansion, defining high-level architecture, module
          boundaries, tech stack selection, and DB schema. Guided a pod of mid-level
          engineers to deliver the platform autonomously with minimal external oversight.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legacy rescue & team management:</strong> Directed a pod of junior engineers
          to stabilize mission-critical legacy systems. Mentored the team on major
          operational upgrades, including remote feature flags and consolidating 20+
          fragmented "branch-per-tenant" repositories into a single CI/CD pipeline.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Engineering culture & "Design-First" documentation:</strong> Institutionalized
          a "Design-First" engineering culture by authoring the organization's standard
          technical Design Document template, ADRs, and backend guidelines. Reduced
          cross-team communication overhead and prevented technical debt across code reviews.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Custom IAM & core domain engineering:</strong> Architected a custom
          Authentication & Access service supporting enterprise SSO, OTP, invites, and
          declarative RBAC to avoid prohibitive licensing costs while optimizing login
          latency. Built the core Content Service and Career Service Booking Engine,
          leveraging RLS for tenant isolation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Infrastructure & CI/CD optimization (AWS CDK):</strong> Conducted code and
          architectural reviews for team AWS CDK infrastructure, executing cost-optimization
          strategies by right-sizing development cloud environments. Enhanced CI/CD pipelines
          to enforce automated quality gates.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="job">
      <h3>Software Engineer — LDUN (Remote, KSA)</h3>
      <p class="when">Jul 2025 – Apr 2026 · part-time</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Closed critical findings from a third-party pentest to meet a fintech security bar.</li>
        <li>Shipped feature and workflow work end-to-end (stability and engagement).</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="job">
      <h3>Software Engineer — Microsoft (Cairo, Egypt)</h3>
      <p class="when">May 2024 – July 2025</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Distributed systems optimization:</strong> Architected a centralized
          orchestration layer to replace a legacy "pull-and-discard" model where 500k+
          domain payloads were redundantly processed by downstream services, resulting in
          a 90% reduction in unnecessary data I/O and eliminating massive cloud compute waste.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cross-org leadership & SLA definition:</strong> Investigated and overhauled
          a failing operational SLA by defining a mathematical priority-tiering system for
          a 500k+ domain ecosystem. Drove cross-organizational alignment across multiple
          teams to adopt the new priority streams, reducing P0/P1 domain processing time
          from 3-5 days to under 6 hours, and boosting the editorial team's throughput by
          600% (from 11 to 80+ domains/week).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data engineering for AI:</strong> Built the automated data ingestion and
          feature-generation pipelines to power a new LLM-based domain classification model.
          Integrated cross-org data feeds and web scraping tools to continuously feed the
          model, diverting traffic from manual review.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Real-time observability:</strong> Transformed operational visibility by
          migrating a rigid, batch-processed daily dashboard to an intuitive, near real-time
          (hourly) analytics platform. Leveraged Kusto (KQL), Cosmos DB, Scope (Data Lake),
          and Power BI to accelerate cross-team decision-making and SLA tracking.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="job">
      <h3>Senior Software Engineer / Software Engineer II / Software Engineer I — Sahl (Giza, Egypt)</h3>
      <p class="when">Dec 2021 – May 2024</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>System scale-up:</strong> Engineered backend and mobile systems to support
          a 40x transaction volume growth, scaling from 2.5k to 100k daily transactions,
          also 16% conversion lift from performance and UX.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Release management & stability:</strong> Owned the mobile app release
          lifecycle. Enforced a strict Feature-Flag deployment strategy, eliminating
          sprint-killing hot-fixes and enabling risk-free rollouts, and data-driven A/B testing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fintech integrations:</strong> Spearheaded complex integrations with major
          telecoms (Vodafone, Orange) and various SMBs, navigating unreliable third-party
          documents and APIs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notification microservice:</strong> Architected a decoupled C# .NET/AWS SQS
          microservice to process millions of push and in-app notifications, supporting
          advanced capabilities like batch sending, scheduling, and in-app deep linking.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Observability & analytics:</strong> Built a custom Flutter event-orchestration
          layer to unify mobile analytics (Mixpanel, GA, FBA), bridging the gap between
          engineering and business by training PMs and Marketing on data-driven decision-making.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Team leadership:</strong> Acted as a core technical leader alongside the L8
          Director, sharing responsibilities for driving sprint planning, managing OKR
          alignment, handling cross-functional syncs, and conducting technical
          interviews/onboarding.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="education-heading">
    <h2 id="education-heading">Education</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li><strong>Cairo University</strong> — Bachelor’s in Computer Engineering (2015 – 2020)</li>
      <li><strong>Udacity</strong> — Nanodegree in Data Analysis (2021)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="extra-heading">
    <h2 id="extra-heading">Extracurricular</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>
        <strong>ACM ICPC Training (2016–2019):</strong> Ranked 37th out of 165 in ACM ECPC 2018,
        advanced to ACPC finals (C++).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Teacher at Dumah Al-Jandal Charitable Org (2009–2015):</strong> Led weekly
        8-hour sessions for ~30 students.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="recs-heading">
    <h2 id="recs-heading">Recommendations</h2>
    <p>
      Available on
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/yahiaabusaif/details/recommendations" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
      — including a Microsoft engineering manager and Sahl / Microsoft teammates.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
